# Consumer-owned schema extension (issue 04 — authorization hooks & membership
# administration). The generated createInvitation / updateInvitation / createMembership
# CRUD mutations remain as low-level primitives, but they expose server-owned
# concerns a client must never set — an Invitation's token, status, invited_by,
# and expiry; a Membership's exact composite key. These three mutations are the
# blessed, safe surface for the invitation and membership lifecycle, mirroring
# how bootstrapWorkspace (issue 03) is preferred over the raw createWorkspace.
#
# Guarding: inviteToWorkspace and revokeInvitation run in the caller's Active
# Workspace, so the authz mutation hook (internal/authz) sees the caller's Role
# and rejects anyone below owner/admin (stories 5, 7). acceptInvitation is the
# exception — the accepting person is not yet a Member, so it authorizes on the
# invitation token instead and mints the Membership with SkipTenancy (story 6),
# the same bootstrap pattern bootstrapWorkspace uses for the first Membership.
#
# Resolver bodies live in membership_admin.resolvers.go and are preserved across
# `sqlgen generate` by gqlgen's copy-through semantics.

"""
Details for inviting a person to the caller's Active Workspace. The invitee is
named only by email — they need not yet have a User account. Everything else
about the Invitation (its token, pending status, issuer, and expiry) is set
server-side.
"""
input InviteToWorkspaceInput {
  "Email address to invite; the invitee accepts by matching it at login"
  email: String!
  "Role the invitee receives on acceptance"
  role: MembershipRole!
}

extend type Mutation {
  """
  Invite a person by email to the Active Workspace with a Role, creating a
  pending Invitation (PRD story 5). Requires an owner/admin Role in the Active
  Workspace — enforced by the authz hook. Returns the created Invitation,
  including the acceptance token.
  """
  inviteToWorkspace(input: InviteToWorkspaceInput!): Invitation!

  """
  Accept a pending Invitation by its token, creating the caller's Membership in
  the invited Workspace and marking the Invitation `accepted` (PRD story 6).
  The caller authenticates as themselves (bearer token) but selects no Active
  Workspace — they are not a Member yet; the token is the authorization. The
  caller's email must match the Invitation's. Returns the new Membership.
  """
  acceptInvitation(token: String!): Membership!

  """
  Revoke a pending Invitation in the Active Workspace so it can no longer be
  accepted (PRD story 7). Requires an owner/admin Role — enforced by the authz
  hook. Only a `pending` Invitation may be revoked. Returns the revoked
  Invitation.
  """
  revokeInvitation(id: UUID!): Invitation!
}
